{# THE RIGHT-NOW STRIP — FOUR TILES OR NONE, like every figure row in
   the product (ruled: four to a row, and five wrapped an orphan onto a
   second line on a small laptop). Every filled tile is a module's: the
   area page lays them out, orders them and counts nothing itself.
   Where a module has not published one, the card keeps its slot and
   says so — a row of two where the design has four is a different
   design, and a reader cannot tell a short row from a quiet morning.

   THE AREA'S OWN TILE IS THE ATTENTION COUNT, which is the one figure
   on this strip the page may state itself: it is the length of a list
   the page already draws. It is the fourth, so the modules fill three:
   the page's own reading of the day keeps its place and the modules
   queue behind it. #}
{% set tiles = nowTiles|slice(0, 3) %}
<div class="grid kstrip ao-kstrip">
    {% for tile in tiles %}
        <div class="c kpi{{ tile.tone == 'hot' ? ' hot' : '' }}{{ tile.tone == 'bad' ? ' bad' : '' }}">
            <span class="tab">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.live %}<span class="src">&middot; <span class="ao-live"><i></i></span></span>{% endif %}</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ tile.value }}{% if tile.unit %}<em>{{ tile.unit }}</em>{% endif %}</b>
            {% if tile.subline %}<span class="sub">{{ tile.subline }}{% if tile.alarm %} &middot; <span class="r">{{ tile.alarm }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
    <div class="c kpi{{ attention is not empty ? ' bad' : '' }}">
        <span class="tab">Needs attention</span>
        <b class="disp">{{ attention|length }}</b>
        {# THE COUNT, BROKEN DOWN: the urgent ones first, then one figure per
           module in the module's own word for its items. Six with no
           breakdown reads as six of something; this says which.

           THE PIECES ARE JOINED, NOT SEPARATED. Writing the dot before each
           piece means working out which piece is first, and the first
           attempt got it wrong the one way that shows: nought urgent, and
           the caption opened with a dot. A count of nought is not a piece
           at all — nobody writes "0 urgent". #}
        {%- set pieces = [] -%}
        {%- if attentionSummary.urgent -%}
            {%- set pieces = pieces|merge(['<span class="r">' ~ attentionSummary.urgent ~ ' urgent</span>']) -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- for label, count in attentionSummary.byModule -%}
            {%- set pieces = pieces|merge([count ~ ' ' ~ label|lower|e]) -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        <span class="sub">{{ attention is empty ? 'a good day' : pieces|join(' &middot; ')|raw }}</span>
    </div>
    {% if tiles|length < 3 %}
        {% for _ in 1..(3 - tiles|length) %}
            <div class="c kpi">
                <span class="tab">From the modules</span>
                <b class="disp">&mdash;</b>
                <span class="sub">no module publishes this</span>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
</div>
